@startuml
title sd — Scheduled maintenance job (hourly, idempotent)
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber
participant "Internal timer\n(runOnce)" as S
participant "Maintenance job" as J
database "Data store\n(via Repositories port)" as D
participant "FileStore" as F

S -> J : runOnce (at startup, then hourly), single instance lock
J -> D : archive PUBLISHED and CANCELLED events whose end passed (J3 D3)
J -> D : lift suspensions whose endsAt passed (AD2)\n+ moderation log + outbox notice
J -> D : drafts untouched 50 weeks without notice:\noutbox notice "deleted in 14 days" (S2)
loop each draft untouched 12 months and notified
  J -> D : re-check it is still untouched (skip if edited)
  J -> F : delete its images (missing file is fine)
  J -> D : then delete the draft, re-checking\n"untouched 12 months" in the delete (S2)
end
J -> D : API keys unused 166 days without notice:\noutbox notice "revoked in 14 days" (I1)
J -> D : API keys unused 180 days and notified: revoke + activity entry (I1)
J -> F : closed associations past 30 days\nwith no active suspension: delete their images first
J -> D : then delete content, log,\ninvitations, keys and closed removal disputes (F2, S1)
J -> D : purge activity entries older than 12 months\nand moderation decisions older than 12 months\nunless linked to an active suspension or open dispute
J -> D : expire PENDING invitations past expiresAt
J --> S : done (each step resumable on next run)
note over J
  Every step is a bounded batch and idempotent:
  a crash mid-run is safe, the next run continues.
  Emails only go through the outbox (Q2).
end note
@enduml
